claim.claim-text:
1. An apparatus for optimization of spectrum utilization in an electromagnetic environment, comprising:
at least one data analysis engine operable to analyze measured data based on the electromagnetic environment to create analyzed data;
wherein the at least one data analysis engine includes a plurality of artificial intelligence (AI) agents;
wherein at least one first AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to make predictions about the electromagnetic environment based on the analyzed data;
wherein at least one second AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to dynamically optimize network parameters based on customer goals and/or customer application requirements; and
wherein at least one third AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to dynamically optimize Layer 1 (L1), Layer 2 (L2), and Layer 3 (L3) functions and/or parameters based on statistical learning techniques and/or control theory.

9. An apparatus for optimization of spectrum utilization in an electromagnetic environment, comprising:
at least one data analysis engine operable to analyze measured data from the electromagnetic environment to create analyzed data;
wherein the at least one data analysis engine includes a plurality of artificial intelligence (AI) agents;
wherein at least one first AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to make predictions about the electromagnetic environment based on the analyzed data;
wherein at least one second AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to interpret a customer goal; and
wherein at least one third AI agent of the plurality of AI agents is operable to dynamically optimize Layer 1 (L1), Layer 2 (L2), and Layer 3 (L3) functions and/or parameters based on statistical learning techniques, the interpreted customer goal, and/or control theory.

16. A method for optimization of spectrum utilization in an electromagnetic environment comprising:
analyzing measured data from the electromagnetic environment to create analyzed data with at least one data analysis engine;
predicting the electromagnetic environment with a plurality of artificial intelligence (AI) agents based on the analyzed data;
interpreting customer goals via at least one first AI agent of the plurality of AI agents; and
dynamically optimizing Layer 1 (L1), Layer 2 (L2), and Layer 3 (L3) functions and/or parameters based on statistical learning techniques, the interpreted customer goals, and/or control theory using at least one second AI agent of the plurality of AI agents.
